WEBVTT

00:00:03.640 --> 00:00:05.360
My voice...

00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:07.510
I was calling you.

00:00:08.290 --> 00:00:09.500
Alice...

00:00:10.150 --> 00:00:12.090
I called you Alice.

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:18.840
To find something I've given up on and
tried to forget in a place like this...

00:00:19.890 --> 00:00:21.860
That's right.

00:00:21.860 --> 00:00:23.210
You are...

00:00:23.210 --> 00:00:24.840
my past!

00:00:26.180 --> 00:00:30.000
Hey, hey! How is that kiddo alive
in space without a space suit?

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:34.220
I'm detecting a faint gravity wave
coming from her surroundings!

00:00:35.240 --> 00:00:38.260
So an airtight layer was formed?

00:00:38.890 --> 00:00:41.680
Orichalt's warp ability could even do that?

00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:44.580
Well, what else could it be then?

00:00:44.580 --> 00:00:46.650
First of all, we have to get Ore...

00:00:46.650 --> 00:00:49.770
...or Alice, I guess, back in the ship!

00:00:51.650 --> 00:00:52.650
No way!

00:00:59.410 --> 00:01:03.180
I have no idea what you want with Alice.

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:06.360
But I'm not handing her over!

00:01:10.410 --> 00:01:12.440
I won't give you my past!

00:02:54.770 --> 00:02:56.720
I won't let Alice go!

00:02:59.410 --> 00:03:02.560
The past I was looking for...

00:03:02.560 --> 00:03:04.520
My reason for living...

00:03:04.520 --> 00:03:06.290
I won't give them up!

00:03:20.240 --> 00:03:21.670
Alice...

00:03:24.160 --> 00:03:28.230
Even our collected Ido is burning with passion now!

00:03:28.230 --> 00:03:29.220
Rick!

00:03:29.220 --> 00:03:31.120
Rampaging outside won't make
their numbers any smaller.

00:03:31.120 --> 00:03:32.730
Let's get out of here now!

00:03:32.730 --> 00:03:33.750
Thanks for that.

00:03:34.250 --> 00:03:35.850
Reflecting on your mistakes?

00:03:35.850 --> 00:03:37.360
Good boy!

00:03:37.360 --> 00:03:38.200
Boss!

00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:40.280
Rick's bringing Ido and the girl back.

00:03:40.280 --> 00:03:42.070
I'll go support them with Fa-Loser.

00:03:42.070 --> 00:03:43.320
I'm counting on you!

00:03:43.320 --> 00:03:44.180
Clair!

00:03:44.180 --> 00:03:46.560
How long until we're out of the cloud?

00:03:46.560 --> 00:03:48.160
Uh, let's see...

00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:51.750
10 minutes until we're out in an area where the
density is low enough to navigate normally.

00:03:51.860 --> 00:03:52.920
Alright!

00:03:52.920 --> 00:03:54.540
We're jumping in exactly 10 minutes.

00:03:55.190 --> 00:03:57.200
Girlie, support Clair.

00:03:57.200 --> 00:03:58.020
Okay!

00:03:58.020 --> 00:03:59.480
Lieutenant, you...

00:03:59.480 --> 00:04:00.530
Captain.

00:04:00.530 --> 00:04:05.390
I'm sure you understand already,
but this unknown substance is after that girl.

00:04:06.560 --> 00:04:10.730
Although, even if it looks like one,
that thing isn't human.

00:04:10.730 --> 00:04:11.890
Abandon her right now!

00:04:11.890 --> 00:04:13.270
Don't be stupid.

00:04:14.170 --> 00:04:19.080
Humans, you know, live for
something inside their hearts.

00:04:19.520 --> 00:04:22.990
That unsociable guy who would
evade people all the time.

00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:26.500
He's staking his life to protect
that brat right now.

00:04:26.500 --> 00:04:27.880
I've known him for a long time.

00:04:27.880 --> 00:04:29.740
I know that bastard's serious.

00:04:29.740 --> 00:04:33.140
And there's nobody on this ship
who wouldn't support him in that.

00:04:33.330 --> 00:04:34.520
Get it?

00:04:34.520 --> 00:04:36.680
We're a family!

00:04:36.680 --> 00:04:40.260
If you're worried about Ido, then instead
of giving dumb suggestions...

00:04:40.260 --> 00:04:42.760
Go get in an I-machine!

00:04:43.480 --> 00:04:46.120
Does an Evertrancer really need one?

00:04:46.120 --> 00:04:47.680
A reason to live.

00:04:48.140 --> 00:04:53.140
Since the day I was born, I've never
thought about a reason for living.

00:04:53.640 --> 00:04:57.200
Just fulfilling duties I'm given, isn't that right?

00:04:57.440 --> 00:04:58.490
Or maybe...

00:04:58.490 --> 00:05:03.050
It's because he's no longer human, but an
Evertrancer that he needs a reason for living?

00:05:03.050 --> 00:05:04.740
If it's a mission, you have to do it!

00:05:04.740 --> 00:05:05.570
Step on it!

00:05:05.570 --> 00:05:08.090
Get in an I-machine and help
out Ido and the rest!

00:05:09.450 --> 00:05:10.940
Uh, me too-

00:05:10.940 --> 00:05:12.900
You have to support Clair, don't you?

00:05:14.370 --> 00:05:15.340
Right.

00:05:17.160 --> 00:05:18.710
Mr. Ido's amazing.

00:05:18.920 --> 00:05:22.840
Even though he's an I-machine,
he stole two ladies' hearts.

00:05:24.060 --> 00:05:24.940
Bridge!

00:05:24.940 --> 00:05:26.000
Hey, bridge!

00:05:26.610 --> 00:05:28.130
Open the airlock.

00:05:28.130 --> 00:05:30.260
I'm letting Alice into the 4th section.

00:05:35.140 --> 00:05:37.020
Stay quiet here for a while.

00:05:45.580 --> 00:05:48.340
Ido, I brought yours too.

00:05:48.340 --> 00:05:49.200
Thanks.

00:05:49.580 --> 00:05:50.670
Tell me.

00:05:50.670 --> 00:05:52.810
Why did you save that girl?

00:05:52.810 --> 00:05:54.600
You into that kind of stuff?

00:05:54.600 --> 00:05:55.310
Stop fooling around.

00:05:55.310 --> 00:05:56.250
Apologies!

00:05:56.250 --> 00:05:59.360
If we're still alive after this,
I'll tell you as much as you want!

00:06:02.100 --> 00:06:03.220
There's no end to them!

00:06:03.220 --> 00:06:05.810
You know, isn't there more
and more of them?

00:06:06.170 --> 00:06:07.240
Imminent gravity wave!

00:06:07.240 --> 00:06:08.460
Multiple objects approaching!

00:06:08.460 --> 00:06:09.300
Why?

00:06:09.300 --> 00:06:12.580
Orichalt's warping more Orichalt in.

00:06:12.580 --> 00:06:16.390
At this rate their mass will keep
increasing geometrically!

00:06:16.390 --> 00:06:17.310
Captain!

00:06:17.310 --> 00:06:19.690
At the current speed they'll catch up with us!

00:06:19.810 --> 00:06:20.600
Clair!

00:06:20.600 --> 00:06:21.690
Emergency jump!

00:06:21.690 --> 00:06:23.000
Papa, you idiot!

00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:24.030
Idiot?

00:06:24.030 --> 00:06:25.030
You don't get it?

00:06:25.030 --> 00:06:26.690
The system's unstable!

00:06:26.690 --> 00:06:28.250
What? Uh...

00:06:28.250 --> 00:06:30.610
I can't emergency jump anywhere, anytime!

00:06:30.610 --> 00:06:32.580
Well, it's because it's like this, you know!

00:06:34.440 --> 00:06:36.400
Something's coming from the front!

00:06:38.340 --> 00:06:39.410
I-machines?

00:06:39.410 --> 00:06:40.360
These are Military!

00:06:40.360 --> 00:06:41.120
What?

00:06:41.120 --> 00:06:41.920
What's their affiliation?

00:06:41.920 --> 00:06:42.900
No idea.

00:06:42.900 --> 00:06:44.590
At a moment like this, seriously?

00:06:44.990 --> 00:06:47.090
They came outside the Miguel Network?

00:06:47.090 --> 00:06:48.250
Are they reinforcements?

00:06:48.840 --> 00:06:52.260
The Military I-machines released
missile-like objects!

00:06:53.560 --> 00:06:55.680
What did our company ever do to them?!

00:06:56.020 --> 00:06:57.280
I'll intercept them!

00:06:57.280 --> 00:06:57.890
Wait.

00:06:58.390 --> 00:07:02.640
They're definitely military-use I-machines,
but they're not the Federation Force's.

00:07:02.640 --> 00:07:06.130
The released objects trajectory
is away from our ship.

00:07:06.130 --> 00:07:07.340
Hear that?

00:07:07.340 --> 00:07:09.800
Looks like they're allies.

00:07:20.780 --> 00:07:21.890
These are!

00:07:21.890 --> 00:07:23.540
T-They're gone.

00:07:23.750 --> 00:07:25.210
Warp weaponry?

00:07:25.210 --> 00:07:26.210
Yeah.

00:07:26.210 --> 00:07:28.210
Designation: TTS.

00:07:28.210 --> 00:07:29.900
Orichalt warp torpedo.

00:07:30.490 --> 00:07:35.720
Performs a Miguel Jump in the midst of the
enemy and forcibly warps them somewhere.

00:07:35.720 --> 00:07:41.010
If the warp coordinate is a star or a black
hole, annihilation is guaranteed.

00:07:41.640 --> 00:07:45.150
Several hundreds of billions' worth
of Orichalt thrown away like that...

00:07:45.660 --> 00:07:48.820
Our allies appear to be really well off, eh.

00:07:48.900 --> 00:07:51.410
We will be out of the cloud in 3 minutes.

00:07:51.410 --> 00:07:52.260
Alright then.

00:07:52.260 --> 00:07:54.450
When we're out, we're cleaning the entire ship.

00:07:54.450 --> 00:07:55.280
Ido!

00:07:55.280 --> 00:07:56.530
You guys as well.

00:07:56.530 --> 00:07:58.920
Just you try leaving a speck of that dust inside.

00:07:58.920 --> 00:08:00.060
I won't go easy on you.

00:08:00.060 --> 00:08:02.120
Treating people like waste matter...

00:08:06.590 --> 00:08:07.550
Captain!

00:08:07.550 --> 00:08:09.800
There's a transmission from
the Military I-machines.

00:08:09.800 --> 00:08:14.170
Coordinates and an Orichalt
transmission decoding key.

00:08:14.170 --> 00:08:16.520
Telling us to jump there, then?

00:08:16.520 --> 00:08:17.890
What are we going to do, Papa?

00:08:17.890 --> 00:08:20.950
Well, they saved us so I guess we
have to show some gratitude.

00:08:20.950 --> 00:08:24.730
Plus, we barely understand anything
about our current situation.

00:08:24.730 --> 00:08:26.510
I want some more info!

00:08:26.510 --> 00:08:27.570
Got it.

00:08:27.820 --> 00:08:33.360
Maybe if we ask them, they'll help us jump
back into the Miguel Net territory!

00:08:33.610 --> 00:08:35.380
You're way too optimistic.

00:08:35.380 --> 00:08:37.880
That's why they made you into a criminal.

00:08:40.540 --> 00:08:43.610
Enough of that, go meet the kid.

00:08:43.610 --> 00:08:46.130
She must be crying there all alone.

00:08:47.140 --> 00:08:48.420
Oh, right!

00:08:48.420 --> 00:08:49.420
I'm off then!

00:08:52.360 --> 00:08:54.230
Maya really is obedient.

00:08:54.230 --> 00:08:55.090
Stupid.

00:08:55.090 --> 00:08:55.800
Oh?

00:08:55.800 --> 00:08:59.480
She's what they call a yes-man.

00:09:04.250 --> 00:09:06.100
Sorry for taking so long.

00:09:11.580 --> 00:09:13.990
Your name is Alice, right?

00:09:16.910 --> 00:09:18.910
Can I call you Alice?

00:09:23.560 --> 00:09:27.210
<i>If Mr. Ido called this girl Alice,</i>

00:09:28.090 --> 00:09:32.090
<i>that means the images back then
were from his past, after all.</i>

00:09:32.600 --> 00:09:35.760
<i>Alice, who appeared from Orichalt
we recovered in that new planet.</i>

00:09:38.140 --> 00:09:41.930
<i>Because of how bizarre of a
phenomenon I bore witness to</i>

00:09:41.930 --> 00:09:45.840
<i>and the situations being serious enough to even
get the Military involved, I end up wondering...</i>

00:09:46.770 --> 00:09:51.700
<i>Just what kind of crime did Mr. Ido commit?</i>

00:10:01.050 --> 00:10:02.760
Miguel Jump complete.

00:10:02.760 --> 00:10:05.210
We're out in normal space.

00:10:05.340 --> 00:10:08.250
Deploying spatial mesh with
Vega as the base coordinate.

00:10:08.250 --> 00:10:10.710
Warp coordinates within expected range.

00:10:16.320 --> 00:10:17.880
There's nothing here.

00:10:18.610 --> 00:10:20.880
You think they fooled us?

00:10:20.880 --> 00:10:26.100
Would there be anyone stupid enough to set
Orichalt at these coordinates just for that?

00:10:26.100 --> 00:10:28.060
Imminent gravity wave detected.

00:10:28.060 --> 00:10:30.020
A massive object is doing a Miguel Out.

00:10:34.440 --> 00:10:35.600
That's...

00:10:35.600 --> 00:10:36.660
The Federation Military?

00:10:37.130 --> 00:10:38.090
It's not.

00:10:38.450 --> 00:10:40.780
That coloring is Observer's.

00:10:40.780 --> 00:10:42.910
By Observer you mean that-

00:10:42.910 --> 00:10:43.990
Yeah.

00:10:43.990 --> 00:10:46.450
A Federation agency that oversees
compliance with treaties.

00:10:47.120 --> 00:10:49.560
A separate unit from the Military.

00:11:02.000 --> 00:11:05.520
This is the treaty compliance agency, Observer.

00:11:05.520 --> 00:11:07.680
Requesting a docking location.

00:11:07.680 --> 00:11:10.840
This is Stulti, affiliated with
the Escavate company.

00:11:10.840 --> 00:11:13.740
Use the 3rd hatch in the 12th block, please.

00:11:13.740 --> 00:11:14.680
Affirmative.

00:11:14.680 --> 00:11:17.010
Let's abide by the treaties.

00:11:17.480 --> 00:11:18.440
Let's get this straight.

00:11:18.440 --> 00:11:21.610
Until we know what they're trying to do, talking about Ore-

00:11:21.610 --> 00:11:22.580
It's Alice.

00:11:22.580 --> 00:11:23.370
What?

00:11:23.370 --> 00:11:24.130
That's her name.

00:11:25.390 --> 00:11:27.700
...talking about Alice is strictly forbidden.

00:11:27.700 --> 00:11:28.660
Got it?

00:11:42.890 --> 00:11:44.330
Lieutenant.

00:11:44.330 --> 00:11:46.040
I'll leave the comms line open.

00:11:46.040 --> 00:11:47.520
I'm leaving her protection to you.

00:11:47.520 --> 00:11:48.650
Got it.

00:11:50.330 --> 00:11:52.840
I thank you for allowing me to board your ship.

00:11:54.260 --> 00:11:57.660
Federation treaty compliance agency, assurance committee,

00:11:57.660 --> 00:12:00.950
3rd inspection group's supervisor Sam Taylor.

00:12:00.950 --> 00:12:02.610
You're alone?

00:12:02.700 --> 00:12:07.500
Please think of it as just an inspection to make
sure you're following the Federation's treaties.

00:12:08.890 --> 00:12:12.250
I have to say though, even with
our investigation abilities,

00:12:12.250 --> 00:12:15.010
finding your ship proved to be
quite an arduous task.

00:12:15.010 --> 00:12:18.300
To think you would be outside the Miguel Net.

00:12:18.300 --> 00:12:20.720
Some trouble occurred during
a Miguel Jump, you see.

00:12:21.050 --> 00:12:24.970
Does that have anything to do with the Federation
Military's ship that tried capturing you?

00:12:25.760 --> 00:12:28.590
Ah, please don't misunderstand.

00:12:28.590 --> 00:12:32.730
I don't intend on causing you any more trouble.

00:12:32.730 --> 00:12:34.780
Well then, what are you here for?

00:12:34.780 --> 00:12:40.490
Our compliance agency has received
info about a high-ranking official

00:12:40.490 --> 00:12:45.810
somehow commanding the Military to recover
Orichalt from a new planet that suddenly appeared.

00:12:45.810 --> 00:12:48.310
We're currently looking into the situation.

00:12:48.660 --> 00:12:51.660
So it wasn't a legitimate operation, after all.

00:12:52.160 --> 00:12:56.130
From what we know, all Escavate
did was take on the request from

00:12:56.130 --> 00:12:59.530
a dummy company to conduct an
excavation at the new planet.

00:12:59.530 --> 00:13:04.260
In other words, you're victims of a fraud.

00:13:04.260 --> 00:13:07.930
So what, you'll let us send them a bill?

00:13:07.930 --> 00:13:11.110
During the investigation,
we noticed something strange.

00:13:11.480 --> 00:13:16.940
They recovered the Orichalt, but why did they
feel the need to capture you as well?

00:13:17.310 --> 00:13:19.900
Dunno, try asking them.

00:13:19.900 --> 00:13:21.690
And one more thing.

00:13:21.690 --> 00:13:24.450
After the excavation, the new planet's satellite-

00:13:24.450 --> 00:13:28.320
No, that entity can't be merely
called a satellite... It attacked.

00:13:28.320 --> 00:13:31.410
That's right, it can't be perceived as
anything but an attack!

00:13:31.410 --> 00:13:36.250
That object attacked, almost as if it had
intelligence or a mind of its own.

00:13:36.250 --> 00:13:38.040
Or could it have been a natural phenomenon?

00:13:38.380 --> 00:13:42.710
Was it drawn in by something and
made to look like that was an attack?

00:13:42.710 --> 00:13:47.710
In any case, this incident is
no mere illegal mining.

00:13:47.710 --> 00:13:50.820
We called in an emergency meeting
and conducted a forced inspection

00:13:50.820 --> 00:13:54.140
of the Military forces that have been
deemed to have violated the treaties.

00:13:54.140 --> 00:13:57.280
We're trying to determine the instigator behind

00:13:57.280 --> 00:14:00.260
the Military's orders and to uncover
the mystery of that new planet.

00:14:00.260 --> 00:14:02.230
Sure thing, do what you want.

00:14:02.230 --> 00:14:06.300
For that, we would like to
request your testimonies.

00:14:06.300 --> 00:14:10.240
Ah. Naturally, we've prepared suitable
compensation for you.

00:14:10.240 --> 00:14:14.960
All records of the illegal actions you've
committed thus far will be erased.

00:14:15.170 --> 00:14:16.600
What do you say?

00:14:17.820 --> 00:14:19.630
Well, that's a mouth-watering offer.

00:14:19.630 --> 00:14:22.010
So you really did do illegal things...

00:14:22.010 --> 00:14:23.220
It was in the gray zone.

00:14:23.220 --> 00:14:24.190
Hm?

00:14:24.630 --> 00:14:25.470
It's fine.

00:14:25.650 --> 00:14:27.360
Is it really?

00:14:27.360 --> 00:14:28.460
Miss Mikuri Maya.

00:14:29.490 --> 00:14:30.100
Yes?

00:14:30.100 --> 00:14:37.140
The false charges about you illegally providing
resource research information can be lifted as well.

00:14:37.690 --> 00:14:39.100
Seriously?

00:14:39.360 --> 00:14:43.400
The person behind this can freely
control the Military.

00:14:43.400 --> 00:14:45.600
I doubt they'll just be sitting and
twiddling their thumbs.

00:14:45.600 --> 00:14:48.610
What if they decide to interfere?

00:14:48.610 --> 00:14:50.070
Please don't worry.

00:14:50.070 --> 00:14:52.450
We'll escort you to the destination.

00:14:53.900 --> 00:14:55.650
Can I talk this over with my crew?

00:14:55.650 --> 00:14:56.970
By all means.

00:14:56.970 --> 00:14:58.850
It's only natural, I would say.

00:15:13.330 --> 00:15:14.890
Well, what do you think?

00:15:14.890 --> 00:15:16.300
I think he's a good guy!

00:15:16.300 --> 00:15:17.740
Smells fishy.

00:15:17.740 --> 00:15:18.800
Definitely a catch there.

00:15:18.800 --> 00:15:20.250
Don't like his tone.

00:15:20.250 --> 00:15:21.520
Hate him in general.

00:15:23.650 --> 00:15:27.120
I think you should be more trusting of people.

00:15:27.120 --> 00:15:33.990
You know, nobody would use stupidly expensive warp
weaponry just to call someone in for questioning.

00:15:34.470 --> 00:15:39.080
Although I guess we can tag along with them
to jump back into the Miguel Net territory.

00:15:39.080 --> 00:15:42.330
And get away from the satellite
chasing us as well.

00:15:42.330 --> 00:15:44.010
I'm against that.

00:15:44.010 --> 00:15:47.010
There's a possibility they'll learn about Alice.

00:15:47.170 --> 00:15:49.050
Ido, let's hear it.

00:15:49.050 --> 00:15:50.220
That Ore-

00:15:50.220 --> 00:15:51.130
It's Alice.

00:15:51.130 --> 00:15:52.340
That's her name.

00:15:52.340 --> 00:15:55.220
That <i>Alice</i>, what's her connection to you?

00:15:55.220 --> 00:15:57.950
I don't exactly know myself.

00:15:57.950 --> 00:16:02.690
But Alice is related to my lost past.

00:16:03.000 --> 00:16:04.860
I'm not giving her to anyone.

00:16:04.860 --> 00:16:07.320
I thought you weren't fixated on your past?

00:16:07.320 --> 00:16:09.490
That's because I had no leads.

00:16:09.490 --> 00:16:12.580
Now that I've found some, I have to find out.

00:16:12.580 --> 00:16:13.700
Even a little.

00:16:13.700 --> 00:16:15.080
Anything.

00:16:16.330 --> 00:16:19.100
But this is selfish, I am aware.

00:16:19.100 --> 00:16:22.400
So I won't ask you to go along with me.

00:16:22.400 --> 00:16:28.420
If you want to accept Observer's offer,
I'll leave the ship with Alice.

00:16:28.420 --> 00:16:30.670
Mr. Ido, you're jumping to
conclusions way too fast!

00:16:30.670 --> 00:16:33.180
Pops, I'm with Ido.

00:16:33.180 --> 00:16:34.470
Me as well.

00:16:34.470 --> 00:16:35.320
Rick.

00:16:35.320 --> 00:16:36.330
Karla.

00:16:39.410 --> 00:16:40.180
Fa-Loser.

00:16:40.180 --> 00:16:41.850
Girlie, you?

00:16:42.040 --> 00:16:43.290
I...

00:16:43.850 --> 00:16:47.370
Think we should protect Alice.

00:16:47.370 --> 00:16:48.980
I second that opinion!

00:16:48.980 --> 00:16:49.860
Ido.

00:16:49.860 --> 00:16:52.490
Forgive me for all of the money
I've borrowed from you, alright?

00:16:52.490 --> 00:16:54.530
Way to ruin the whole scene.

00:16:54.530 --> 00:16:55.810
My bad!

00:16:57.660 --> 00:16:59.650
How did you come to this decision?

00:16:59.650 --> 00:17:03.160
This ship is being chased by both the Military and an unknown satellite.

00:17:03.160 --> 00:17:05.830
You're putting your lives in danger!

00:17:06.040 --> 00:17:09.710
We're miners, our lives are always in danger.

00:17:09.710 --> 00:17:14.040
Not really that different from
going into a Level 4 storm.

00:17:14.040 --> 00:17:15.060
Yeah, yeah.

00:17:15.060 --> 00:17:16.580
You good-for-nothings...

00:17:16.580 --> 00:17:21.590
Honestly, there's guaranteed
to be a catch to this deal.

00:17:22.210 --> 00:17:24.200
There's the genius fund manager's intuition!

00:17:24.200 --> 00:17:26.570
As expected from someone in this
business for 10-something yea-

00:17:27.310 --> 00:17:29.160
Let's not talk about age.

00:17:29.160 --> 00:17:30.980
My bad.

00:17:31.490 --> 00:17:34.770
Alright, now that we've come to a conclusion-

00:17:36.030 --> 00:17:37.870
Gravity wave fluctuation?

00:17:37.870 --> 00:17:38.910
Could it be?

00:17:38.910 --> 00:17:44.650
Observer's interstellar ship is trying to
Miguel Jump with our Stulti in tow?

00:17:48.950 --> 00:17:50.470
Hey hey hey hey!

00:17:50.470 --> 00:17:52.670
That's a very forced way of escorting!

00:17:52.670 --> 00:17:54.820
That bastard got us!

00:17:54.820 --> 00:17:56.550
The Observer person is missing!

00:17:57.110 --> 00:17:59.340
Why did they-

00:18:00.600 --> 00:18:02.720
Eh? Alice disappeared?

00:18:03.180 --> 00:18:05.900
So they knew about her from the start?!

00:18:05.900 --> 00:18:07.990
There's a response from the
corridor to the shuttle!

00:18:08.480 --> 00:18:09.370
Got it!

00:18:10.980 --> 00:18:14.170
You're a lady, you ought to be
a little more graceful.

00:18:15.740 --> 00:18:17.160
If talking doesn't work, then-

00:18:17.160 --> 00:18:18.090
Stop right there.

00:18:18.960 --> 00:18:22.610
Telling someone to stop in zero gravity
is asking for the impossible now, isn't it?

00:18:23.160 --> 00:18:25.830
Was that girl your target from the start?

00:18:26.660 --> 00:18:28.420
Lieutenant Amanza.

00:18:28.420 --> 00:18:31.250
You're considered a deserter, you know?

00:18:31.250 --> 00:18:32.220
What?

00:18:32.220 --> 00:18:38.090
A traitor who went AWOL and is collaborating with
former Captain Jake Hojo, who now goes by Grayman.

00:18:38.090 --> 00:18:38.680
You lie!

00:18:38.680 --> 00:18:39.980
It's the truth.

00:18:39.980 --> 00:18:43.600
However, I could restore you
to your former position.

00:18:43.600 --> 00:18:45.170
Are you trying to fool me?

00:18:45.170 --> 00:18:46.610
Of course not.

00:18:46.610 --> 00:18:49.010
Mikuri Maya. Don't you see?

00:18:49.010 --> 00:18:52.220
We can create the truth without
having to fool anyone

00:18:52.220 --> 00:18:54.780
But why restore me to the Military?

00:18:54.980 --> 00:18:56.740
It's necessary for you, right?

00:18:56.740 --> 00:19:01.450
You're powerless in life without a
social position, after all.

00:19:01.450 --> 00:19:04.080
So you can read me like a book?

00:19:04.080 --> 00:19:05.030
Indeed.

00:19:06.410 --> 00:19:08.970
What if I still tell you to surrender?

00:19:08.970 --> 00:19:11.300
Obviously, I'll do this.

00:19:11.750 --> 00:19:13.670
I'm confident in my shooting skills.

00:19:13.670 --> 00:19:14.940
What a coincidence.

00:19:14.940 --> 00:19:16.230
Me too.

00:19:16.920 --> 00:19:18.180
Supervisor!

00:19:18.180 --> 00:19:19.090
What is it?

00:19:19.090 --> 00:19:21.290
Multiple imminent gravity waves detected.

00:19:21.290 --> 00:19:22.760
During a Miguel Jump?

00:19:23.010 --> 00:19:24.680
Did they come?

00:19:29.850 --> 00:19:31.220
Dammit!

00:19:34.680 --> 00:19:36.090
Wait!

00:19:36.090 --> 00:19:37.760
Release Alice!

00:19:38.910 --> 00:19:40.360
Just wonderful.

00:19:41.070 --> 00:19:43.570
Take me to the shuttle, please.

00:19:44.600 --> 00:19:46.990
Multiple objects have warped
into the Miguel Line.

00:19:47.260 --> 00:19:48.330
Code Red.

00:19:48.330 --> 00:19:50.000
I-machines, prepare for interception.

00:19:51.220 --> 00:19:52.480
Huh?

00:19:52.480 --> 00:19:54.290
Why the Observer ship?

00:19:54.290 --> 00:19:56.250
Weren't they aiming for the kiddo?

00:19:56.250 --> 00:19:57.780
What's going on?

00:19:59.400 --> 00:20:00.250
Clair.

00:20:00.250 --> 00:20:04.430
I feel bad for Observer, but we should do an
emergency jump and escape while we can.

00:20:04.430 --> 00:20:05.280
Papa!

00:20:05.280 --> 00:20:07.610
The 11th shuttle has gone into
the launch sequence!

00:20:07.610 --> 00:20:08.670
What?

00:20:14.860 --> 00:20:16.900
My apologies.

00:20:16.900 --> 00:20:18.970
I don't have a license, see.

00:20:18.970 --> 00:20:22.040
What are you going to do with Alice?

00:20:22.040 --> 00:20:23.360
Research her, of course.

00:20:23.360 --> 00:20:26.160
Your ship is taking damage, you know!

00:20:26.160 --> 00:20:28.610
We have escape measures ready.

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:32.040
I'm not giving you Alice.

00:20:32.280 --> 00:20:33.370
Mr. Ido!

00:20:33.780 --> 00:20:35.500
I'm taking Alice back.

00:20:38.000 --> 00:20:40.420
What is this biological signal?

00:20:40.420 --> 00:20:42.410
What's someone like that doing
on this mining ship...

00:20:43.380 --> 00:20:44.150
Could it be?

00:20:44.150 --> 00:20:45.530
Impossible!

00:20:45.530 --> 00:20:47.050
You were alive?!

00:20:47.050 --> 00:20:49.390
You bastard, you know me?

00:20:49.390 --> 00:20:50.350
Answer me!

00:20:50.720 --> 00:20:51.940
Who am I?

00:20:51.940 --> 00:20:53.630
What did I do in the past?

00:20:54.420 --> 00:20:55.900
Ido, evade!

00:21:00.320 --> 00:21:01.730
Alice!

00:21:08.450 --> 00:21:09.580
Stay away!

00:21:11.420 --> 00:21:12.790
W-Wait!

00:21:12.790 --> 00:21:14.240
That girl and that man with you-

00:21:15.930 --> 00:21:17.000
Mr. Ido!

00:21:17.000 --> 00:21:18.180
Catch us please!

00:21:24.640 --> 00:21:26.920
A man who knew my past...

00:21:27.530 --> 00:21:28.740
What?

00:21:30.260 --> 00:21:37.260
Ido!

00:23:12.450 --> 00:23:14.200
My name is Sam Taylor.

00:23:14.200 --> 00:23:18.160
This is hard to believe, but I witnessed
someone who I think might be him.

00:23:18.160 --> 00:23:20.410
If he's alive, he must be exterminated!

00:23:20.410 --> 00:23:20.940
He's...

00:23:20.940 --> 00:23:23.000
He's an enemy of mankind!

00:23:25.780 --> 00:23:28.300
Everything is inside the ore.

00:23:28.560 --> 00:23:32.220
Wishes and bonds are all locked
in the world of minerals.

00:23:32.480 --> 00:23:39.810
Will the thing to break that silence be definite
friendship or a trifling attachment?
